OL,3,GNEWSADisbelief as 'most important item'
OL,4,Afound under bed
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe "most important item" ever to be
OL,7,Fsold at an auction house is about to go
OL,8,Funder the hammer after being found
OL,9,Funder a bed, an auctioneer has said
OL,11,FA newly discovered head of a thylacine,
OL,12,Falso known as a Tasmanian Tiger, was
OL,13,Fdug out from the owner's storage after
OL,14,Fthey saw a similar specimen make the
OL,15,Fnews in August.
OL,17,FNicknamed Trevor, the new specimen is
OL,18,F"only the third known taxidermy
OL,19,FThylacine head in existence" and could
OL,20,Fsell for up to #50,000, according to
OL,21,FBristol auction house Auctioneum.
OL,23,APub: 28-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
FL,342,340,200,160,0,100
